them from the Music Technology Group (UPF) and pins each file by SHA-256.

## Models

Source: <https://essentia.upf.edu/models.html>

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `discogs-effnet-bsdynamic-1.onnx` | EffNet embeddings for the tag heads |
| `msd-musicnn-1.onnx` | MusiCNN embeddings for valence/arousal |
| `mood_happy-discogs-effnet-1.onnx` | happy / not happy |
| `mood_sad-discogs-effnet-1.onnx` | sad / not sad |
| `mood_aggressive-discogs-effnet-1.onnx` | aggressive / not aggressive |
| `mood_relaxed-discogs-effnet-1.onnx` | relaxed / not relaxed |
| `mood_party-discogs-effnet-1.onnx` | party / not party |
| `danceability-discogs-effnet-1.onnx` | danceable / not danceable |
| `deam-msd-musicnn-2.onnx` | valence and arousal (DEAM) |

Licence: the MTG models page states **CC BY-NC-SA 4.0**; the MTG licensing page states
**CC BY-NC-ND 4.0**. The two pages disagree, but both restrict use to non-commercial
purposes, and MTG offers a proprietary licence on request. Because the application relies on
these weights, the combined application is non-commercial.

